  "title": "Chickpea Salad with Feta Cheese",
  "description": "The feta cheese is already salty enough, so salt the salad lightly.",
  "editorial": {
    "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The chickpea Salad with Feta Cheese is a very simple salad, composed of canned chickpeas and feta. The tomatoes and bell peppers are not necessary, but provide more flavor and vitamins, as well as a vibrant color.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe {\"id\":21244,\"template\":\"chic-template-english\",\"updated\":1659213468695} -->\n<!--WPRM Recipe 21244-->\n<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe\">\n\t<h2 class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-name\">Chickpea Salad with Feta Cheese</h2>\n\t<img class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-image\" src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/05/IMG_9818.Blog_-150x150.png\"/>\t<p class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-summary\">\n\t\tThe feta cheese is already salty enough, so salt the salad lightly.\r\n\t</p>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-equipment\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-ingredients\">\n\t\t<ul><li>400 g (1 can)  garbanzo beans (drained)</li><li>150 g feta cheese (cubed)</li><li>15 cherry tomatoes, or 2 medium tomatoes (sliced)</li><li>1 bell pepper (cored and sliced)</li><li>1/2 red onion (cut into thin slices)</li><li>1 clove garlic (pressed)</li><li>Fresh or dried herbs (cilantro, chive, dill) (chopped)</li><li>Salt and freshly ground black pepper</li><li>1 lemon (juice only)</li><li>3-4 Tbsp olive oil</li></ul>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-instructions\">\n\t\t<ol><li>In a salad bowl, mix the chickpea, feta, tomatos, bell pepper, onion, garlic, and herbs.\r\n</li><li>Season with salt and pepper. Drizzle with freshly pressed lemon juice and olive oil. Serve right away or keep it in the refrigerator.\r\n<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/05/IMG_9817.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li></ol>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-notes\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n</div>\n<!--End WPRM Recipe-->\n<!-- /wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe -->",
    "excerpt": null
  },
